# Project context folder

Long-lived facts live in `context/` so chats do not need to rediscover them.

- Before re-investigating hosting, tunnels, or APK ↔ API wiring, read `context/hosting-mvp.md`.
- For stack / request paths, read `context/architecture.md`.
- For day-to-day demo commands, read `context/runbook.md`.

When you learn a durable fact (how hosting works, a non-obvious bugfix, env layout),
update the matching file under `context/` instead of only saying it in chat.

Never put secrets in `context/`.
